---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service · neondeck"
  description="The basic terms for using neondeck.dev and the open-source Neondeck project."
>
  <div class="site-shell">
    <SiteNav />
    <main class="container terms-page">
      <p class="kicker">TERMS · NEONDECK.DEV</p>
      <h1>Use the site responsibly. Keep control of your tools.</h1>
      <p class="terms-lede">
        These terms govern your use of neondeck.dev. Neondeck itself is
        open-source software licensed separately under the MIT License.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Using this site</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing neondeck.dev, you agree to these terms. You may use the
          site only in compliance with applicable law and may not attempt to
          disrupt, damage, or gain unauthorized access to the site or its
          supporting systems. If you do not agree, do not use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Open-source software</h2>
        <p>
          The Neondeck software and its source code are provided under the
          <a href="https://github.com/pandemicsyn/neondeck/blob/main/LICENSE"
            >MIT License</a
          >. That license—not these site terms—governs your right to use, copy,
          modify, distribute, or sell the software. If these terms conflict with
          the MIT License about the software, the MIT License controls.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your environment and actions</h2>
        <p>
          Neondeck runs in infrastructure you control and can interact with
          repositories, shells, credentials, AI providers, and other developer
          services you configure. You are responsible for securing that
          environment, reviewing permissions and proposed changes, keeping
          appropriate backups, and deciding whether generated output or an
          automated action is suitable for your use.
        </p>
        <p>
          Agent output may be incomplete, incorrect, or unsafe. Review code,
          commands, pull-request activity, and other consequential output before
          relying on it or sending it to a third party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Neondeck can connect to services such as GitHub and AI model
          providers. Those services are operated by others and are governed by
          their own terms, privacy policies, availability, and charges. You are
          responsible for your accounts and for complying with their terms.
          Neondeck does not control or endorse third-party services merely by
          supporting an integration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Neondeck is evolving software and may include beta or experimental
          features. The site, documentation, and project may change, be
          interrupted, or be discontinued without notice. Documentation may
          occasionally be incomplete or out of date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>No warranties</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, neondeck.dev and its content
          are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any
          kind, express or implied. The Neondeck software carries the separate
          warranty disclaimer in the MIT License.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, Neondeck’s authors and
          contributors will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or exemplary damages, or for lost data, profits,
          goodwill, or business interruption arising from your use of, or
          inability to use, the site. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
          limitations, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated as the project changes. Material updates
          will be reflected on this page with a new effective date. Continuing
          to use the site after an update means you accept the revised terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Open a discussion or issue in the
          <a href="https://github.com/pandemicsyn/neondeck"
            >Neondeck repository</a
          >. These terms are effective August 24, 2026.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms-page {
    max-width: 820px;
    padding-block: clamp(70px, 10vw, 120px);
  }

  .terms-page h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    text-align: left;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .terms-lede {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 28px 0 70px;
    color: var(--body);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .terms-page section {
    padding-block: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .terms-page h2 {
    margin: 0 0 15px;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.15rem);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .terms-page section p {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .terms-page section p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }

  .terms-page section a {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .terms-page h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 13vw, 4rem);
    }

    .terms-lede {
      margin-bottom: 48px;
      font-size: 17px;
    }
  }
</style>
